  "details": "This package provides a server-side implementation of the FIDO Device Onboard (FDO) specification, written in Go. FDO is an open standard for the late binding of device credentials, allowing for automated and secure on-boarding of devices when they are first powered on in their final location.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * encoding/asn1: golang: Go encoding/asn1: Denial of Service via excessive recursion in Unmarshal (CVE-2026-33818)\n  * net/[http](http): golang: Go net/[http](http): Unencrypted HTTP/2 connections vulnerable to Denial of Service (CVE-2026-56853)\n  * crypto/tls: golang: Golang crypto/tls: Denial of Service via indefinite KeyUpdate messages (CVE-2026-56862)\n  * crypto/tls: golang: crypto/tls: Denial of Service via multiple ECH outer extension references (CVE-2026-97031)\n  * net/[http](http): net/http/internal/http2: golang.org/x/net/http2: net/[http](http): Denial of Service via excessive HTTP/2 SETTINGS frames (CVE-2026-78669)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
